<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU VISIT</span><h1>A few helpful things to know.</h1><p>Plan a comfortable visit to Materuni Village with practical information from your local hosts.</p></section>
<section class="section"><div class="split"><div><h2>Getting to Materuni</h2><p>Materuni Village is in the Kilimanjaro foothills, near Moshi. Transport from Moshi is not included in the listed package prices unless specifically agreed. Confirm your pickup point and transport arrangements when booking.</p><h2>What to bring</h2><p>Comfortable walking shoes, light rain protection, sun protection, a reusable water bottle and a camera. The waterfall trail can be wet or uneven, so choose footwear with good grip.</p><h2>Food and dietary needs</h2><p>Local meals are part of several experiences. Please tell us about allergies, dietary preferences or accessibility needs when you send your booking request.</p></div><div><h2>Booking and payment</h2><p>Send a booking request with your preferred date and group size. We will check arrangements and contact you with confirmation and payment instructions. Submitting a request does not take payment or guarantee a confirmed booking.</p><h2>Weather and waterfall conditions</h2><p>Conditions vary by season. Water levels, trail conditions and opportunities to swim depend on the weather and local safety conditions on the day.</p><h2>Need a hand?</h2><p>Talk directly with Materuni Hosts.</p><a class="button" href="https://wa.me/255612068540" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a></div></div></section>
